1
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,240
A strange feeling

2
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:47,700
So I walked along the arcade guide tiles

3
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
stepping only on the black ones.

4
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

5
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,620
but everyone's forgotten.

6
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:05,780
Politicians with their pompous faces,

7
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:09,080
and the aunties who
are a thorn in your side,

8
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:12,080
try turning the corner.

9
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,660
That corner there.

10
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,880
You'll meet everyone, everyone!

11
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:24,500
Over there is Kameari,

12
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:27,820
surely Kameari!

13
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:32,980
Everyone, come to our town!

14
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:34,640
Thank you.

15
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:40,780
This is the story of an autumn when
our senior saw both heaven and hell.

16
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:45,280
The story began at the autumn art exhibition
hosted by the Katsushika Police Station.

17
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:54,240
Quite a turnout, isn't it, Ohara-kun?

18
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:58,480
Our station's art exhibition, which we
started to foster exchange with local residents,

19
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,180
seems to be finally gaining recognition,
does it not?

20
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:05,760
They're all truly wonderful works.

21
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:09,060
Why, this one looks like a professional's work,
doesn't it?

22
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:15,700
Coming from you, Chairman, someone so
knowledgeable about art, we're truly honored.

23
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:17,180
And Hara-kun,

24
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:22,900
yes, this one is a work by Nakagawa
Jun from our Yaeshiro station.

25
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:27,080
He has been formally studying
painting since he was a small child.

26
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:27,980
I see, I see.

27
00:02:28,820 --> 00:02:32,220
This is also a work by
our Officer Reiko Akimoto.

28
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:34,920
Well, this is a masterful ink painting.

29
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:37,100
Indeed, it's the real thing.

30
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:40,580
This is also a work by our Officer Terai.

31
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:43,340
Hara-kun.

32
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:46,320
Are you planning to introduce
everyone's work in the station?

33
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:47,520
Sorry about that.

34
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:50,940
Everyone worked hard,
squeezing this in between their duties.

35
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:51,740
It's hot!

36
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:52,980
Not at all.

37
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:53,860
It's finished.

38
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:58,140
Is this also a work from
the Katsushika station?

39
00:02:59,540 --> 00:02:59,980
This is...

40
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,340
Free pass...

41
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:02,560
Ohara-kun.

42
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:05,060
We were supposed to keep
this a secret from that guy.

43
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,080
That's what I was sure of, too.

44
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,980
What happened?

45
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:13,560
This seems to have been put up by mistake.

46
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,500
Ohara-kun.

47
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,840
I'll clear it away right now.

48
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,600
Move, move, move, move!

49
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:26,600
Coming through, coming through!

50
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:29,860
Okay, this spot should do.

51
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:30,020
Yes.

52
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,540
Hey, Ryotsu! What on earth do
you think you're doing here?

53
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,180
That's uncalled for, Chief!

54
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:41,320
Why did you keep the art
exhibition a secret from me?

55
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,740
W-well, that's...

56
00:03:42,740 --> 00:03:45,820
Senpai, where should I put this?

57
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:47,040
Let me see.

58
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:49,760
Put it over here.

59
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,100
Yes.

60
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:51,840
What are you doing?

61
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:55,220
We're displaying my entries.

62
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:57,880
My works this time are amazing.

63
00:03:58,380 --> 00:03:59,588
First, paintings,

64
00:03:59,638 --> 00:04:02,660
then sculptures and many crafts.

65
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:06,840
And this year's highlight,
a battleship made of matchboxes!

66
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:12,160
From now on,
please call me the Da Vinci of Katsushika.

67
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:14,280
What's this...

68
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:14,820
Hey!

69
00:04:15,340 --> 00:04:18,160
Don't you dare touch my art so casually,
old man!

70
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,620
Old man?

71
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:24,440
Excuse me, we have tea ready,
so please come this way.

72
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:28,080
Ohara, do something about this!

73
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:30,020
That...

74
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:35,200
Ryotsu, please, just today,
don't get in the way.

75
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:37,140
What do you mean by that?

76
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:40,700
I'm just cooperating with the art exhibition,
aren't I?

77
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:45,900
Listen,
calm down and take a good look around.

78
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:49,900
Your piece is obviously the only one sticking out in this venue,
isn't it?

79
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:52,580
Can't you see it's disrupting
the harmony of the space?

80
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:55,920
That's what art is, Chief.

81
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,640
Art always disrupts the
atmosphere of a place,

82
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:01,800
and it brings down the
values that restrict us.

83
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:04,160
But, well...

84
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,780
Your work is...

85
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:09,580
Last year it was a plastic model
tank with a blonde female figure.

86
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:12,420
And the year before,
a cosplay show of tokusatsu heroes.

87
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:16,200
And this year, I made the
battleship Yamato out of matchsticks.

88
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:19,740
This has nothing to do with art at all,
does it?

89
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:21,500
No, it's not, Chief.

90
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:24,580
This isn't Yamato, it's Musashi.

91
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:30,040
They're nearly identical, but the number of secondary
turrets and triple-mount machine guns is different.

92
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:33,360
This man is so picky about these details.

93
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:35,480
What do you mean, picky?

94
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:39,020
You corrected me because I said something wrong,
didn't you?

95
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:44,340
People like you always say
"Zero" the moment they see a fighter plane.

96
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:48,260
But the Goshikisen and the Hayabusa look alike,
yet they're totally different planes.

97
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:50,500
Please stop being so vague.

98
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:54,280
You're a police officer,
so please use proper Japanese.

99
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,880
Wow, this is awesome.

100
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:57,600
Seriously, it's so cool.

101
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,140
I want this one.

102
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:02,240
Look, Chief.

103
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:06,200
Innocent hearts can see the value in my work,
can't they?

104
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:11,120
Isn't a work like this
what true art really is?

105
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:15,300
Listen, Ryotsu.

106
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:19,800
Art is paintings like these,
the ones Nakagawa and Reiko made.

107
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:23,020
Compared to these,
your paintings are nothing but doodles.

108
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:23,900
Doodles?

109
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,900
Then let me ask you, Chief.

110
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:29,380
What exactly makes Nakagawa's
and Reiko's paintings art?

111
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:34,980
But Nakagawa and Reiko have had top
art instructors since they were children.

112
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:40,920
They've studied, visited art museums all over the world,
and built up their refinement.

113
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,820
They're on a different level from you.
A completely different level.

114
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:48,040
Does getting a gifted education
bought with money make something art?

115
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:52,380
Are you saying artists can't
come from poor families, Chief?

116
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:56,480
That's not what I meant at all.

117
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:58,200
Then what do you mean?

118
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:00,760
So Nakagawa's and Reiko's
paintings are art, and

119
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:04,260
what's your basis for
calling my painting a doodle?

120
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:11,260
Didn't I hear that you two have gotten into the art exhibition before,
somehow?

121
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:13,880
That's right, that's right.

122
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:19,720
Nakagawa-kun's and Reiko-kun's works have a track
record of being recognized as art by the public.

123
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,040
That's the basis for it.

124
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:24,820
Wouldn't you be better suited
to show business than art?

125
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:26,900
Like going on about what
Madame Debi did or whatever.

126
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:28,760
Or the Kano sisters and all that.

127
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,340
Don't belittle show business, please.

128
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:34,460
Can you have an affair in art?

129
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:36,660
Can you?

130
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,640
Hey, hey.

131
00:07:38,640 --> 00:07:40,280
Your goddamn corner!

132
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:42,080
Stop it, stop it!

133
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:46,580
This bastard!

134
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:47,760
Let go, you bastard!

135
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:48,780
Ugh, what a pain.

136
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:51,540
I just can't do this anymore.

137
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:52,880
Maybe today's the day.

138
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,820
Ryotsu-kun too.

139
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:57,240
You get your own special corner,

140
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,600
so I'll let you have it.

141
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:12,140
It's like a classic.

142
00:08:12,140 --> 00:08:16,020
Your work has a strong personality,
so this placement is probably better.

143
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:20,140
Singling you out like this,
the others might resent it, you know.

144
00:08:20,140 --> 00:08:22,420
Good for you, senpai.

145
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:24,500
I'm sorry, Chief.

146
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:28,140
Unlike some people,
you really are understanding, Chief.

147
00:08:28,140 --> 00:08:30,160
What's with that snide tone?

148
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:32,300
Ohara, that's enough!

149
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:33,760
Sorry.

150
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:07,620
What do you mean, you don't know?

151
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:10,120
Don't blame me for that.

152
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:12,500
The thing I stayed up all night to finish!

153
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:16,600
Well, during the art exhibition,
Senpai's work

154
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:20,580
seems to have been kept behind
a screen so no one would see it.

155
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:24,380
So this year,
the Chief has finally given up on you

156
00:09:24,380 --> 00:09:26,780
What's that supposed to mean?

157
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:31,820
Well, honestly, Ryo-san's work is a bit...

158
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:35,040
For a work to be displayed
at an art exhibition,

159
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:38,460
you should just enjoy it as a hobby,
don't you think?

160
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:39,300
Right?

161
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:44,020
All of you, lining up together to insult me!

162
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:48,620
I'll tell you this, Ryo-chan.
Art isn't that easy.

163
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:49,540
It's not something you can just do.

164
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:49,700
That's right.

165
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:54,880
Even among painters called masters, some were
never recognized at all during their lifetimes.

166
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:55,700
That's how it is.

167
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:56,580
Right?

168
00:09:57,460 --> 00:10:02,000
So it's the same for me. Nobody is willing to recognize me,
and if this goes on, my

169
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:06,440
senior's talent will be buried. Don't you think
it would be a huge loss to Japan's art world?

170
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:08,260
Don't be so dramatic.

171
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:11,760
Then why don't you enter an art exhibition too,
Ryo-chan?

172
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:12,960
That's right.

173
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:16,700
Then everyone would recognize your talent,
wouldn't they?

174
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:17,780
Right?

175
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:19,060
I see.

176
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:23,840
Alright, in that case I'll get
into a famous art exhibition.

177
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,340
Just you wait, Chief and Chief.

178
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:29,700
I'll definitely show you two up.

179
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:33,000
With my painting, I'm sure to get in.

180
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:34,740
What confidence!

181
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:37,340
Did we make a mistake by
getting him all fired up?

182
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:41,200
No matter how you think about it,
that painting is never going to get in.

183
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:44,140
When you think about what
happens if he's rejected...

184
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:54,620
There are an awful lot of entries this year.

185
00:10:54,620 --> 00:10:55,820
They really are.

186
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:58,760
So this is the painting
by Master Akatsuka's son?

187
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:01,040
A 100% acceptance rate.

188
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:03,680
This is the highlight of this exhibition.

189
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:05,880
The selection committee is about to begin.

190
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:07,020
Yes.

191
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:13,060
Then start with the works near the entrance.

192
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:14,300
Carry them to the venue in order.

193
00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:14,900
Understood.

194
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:20,340
Since we wouldn't want any mix-ups.

195
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:22,880
Should we move the rejected
works to another room?

196
00:11:23,300 --> 00:11:23,660
Yes, I suppose we should.

197
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,660
Tch, that's dangerous on top of the feet.

198
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:36,280
Hey! This is the work
of Master Akatsuka's son!

199
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:39,160
Isn't that the spot
for the rejected entries?

200
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:42,600
We almost rejected it by mistake.
Whew, that was close.

201
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:49,060
There's a Nanase painting in
the new candidates, though.

202
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:51,420
What's with this shelf for bad paintings?

203
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:53,080
Just leave that somewhere.

204
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:54,520
Yeah, you're right.

205
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:02,660
Number 52, this is the work of
Yoshihiro Miyagawa from Shibuya Ward.

206
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,500
It's a poor year this year.

207
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:07,660
Yeah, it really is terrible.

208
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:11,680
I heard there's a painting by Master
Akatsuka's son this year, though.

209
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:14,040
Does that make it lacking?

210
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:16,620
Especially since no gold prizes have
been awarded in the last few years.

211
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:24,040
This one's still no good.

212
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:27,240
I'll take some water.
I'm going to take some stomach medicine.

213
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:31,240
Number 53. This piece is

214
00:12:31,290 --> 00:12:33,980
by the son of the eminent painter Akatsuka.

215
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:34,640
Eeeh!

216
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:36,100
W-which one?

217
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:42,187
It's truly a sanabullet, a wonderful talent!

218
00:12:42,237 --> 00:12:43,820
What do you all think?

219
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:47,432
Yes, indeed. Among the entries this time,

220
00:12:47,482 --> 00:12:49,680
I sense a truly outstanding individuality.

221
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:53,380
I sense something extraordinary in
the bold brushwork and composition.

222
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:56,960
So we're all in agreement, then?

223
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:57,560
Hey.

224
00:12:58,460 --> 00:13:00,120
Gold prize it is.

225
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,120
Excuse me, just a moment.

226
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:07,720
I heard a gold prize was awarded
for the first time in five years.

227
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:09,540
Is that the work?

228
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:12,440
Yes, a magnificent work has emerged.

229
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:16,000
Excuse me,
could you bring the work over here?

230
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:17,380
Yeah, yeah.

231
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:20,300
This is the gold prize-winning work.

232
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:37,040
What, that painting is the wrong one?

233
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:40,400
Yes, it seems the name plates got swapped.

234
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:42,740
Then what happened to the real one?

235
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:44,600
And the all-important painting by the...

236
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:47,700
It seems they thought it was
rejected and threw it away.

237
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:48,620
They threw it away?

238
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:51,360
It seems it wasn't marked
as wanting to be exhibited.

239
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:53,420
Please do this one too.

240
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:58,020
We'll just have to push through
with this clumsy painting.

241
00:13:58,020 --> 00:14:01,240
Let's pretend the master's
painting never arrived.

242
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:01,780
No way.

243
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:05,840
Who on earth is the artist of that work?

244
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:09,420
It's Kankichi Ryotsu of Katsushika Ward.

245
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,960
First submission, first acceptance.

246
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:22,240
And on top of that,
he's a active police officer,

247
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:26,233
so the media covered him extensively,

248
00:14:26,283 --> 00:14:29,771
and the public buzzed about the
arrival of a major new painter,

249
00:14:29,821 --> 00:14:32,180
and Senpai has truly
become the talk of the town.

250
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:35,864
Now, tonight we have the
hottest topic of the moment,

251
00:14:35,914 --> 00:14:38,680
Mr. Ryo Tsukankichi!

252
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:40,721
Good evening, everyone.

253
00:14:40,771 --> 00:14:43,340
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu,
the one everyone's talking about.

254
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:47,956
W-why?

255
00:14:48,006 --> 00:14:50,740
Why is this painting the gold prize?

256
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,560
It's starting to look like a good piece,
isn't it?

257
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:55,520
Yeah.

258
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:57,740
When you think about it, artists are...

259
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:58,720
like Ryo-san.

260
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,340
There are a lot of unconventional people,
aren't there?

261
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:02,280
Bonjour!

262
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:04,400
Hello, everyone at Hassuja.

263
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:05,140
Yuka.

264
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:07,500
W-what's with that outfit?

265
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:09,460
Where's your uniform? Where's your uniform?

266
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:10,740
Hey!

267
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:12,160
Who's that over there?

268
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:13,540
at that art exhibition,

269
00:15:13,540 --> 00:15:15,380
where your artistic talent was recognized,

270
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:17,940
my work, the gold prize winner,

271
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:19,320
you called a mere doodle.

272
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:21,280
Why, isn't that Chief Ohara?

273
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:28,180
Thanks to you,
that doodle sold for 5 million yen.

274
00:15:28,180 --> 00:15:29,120
5 million yen.

275
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:34,240
After all,
the public has recognized that I'm a genius.

276
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:36,880
I have that kind of track record, you know.

277
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:40,160
Now I'm a treasure of the art world.

278
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:42,860
They're really giving you a hard time,
aren't they?

279
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:47,440
You'd absolutely never want to pass that along,
would you?

280
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:48,820
They say entertainment suits you better.

281
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:53,500
The Chief's calling for you.

282
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:56,880
Ryotsu-kun, congratulations!

283
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:59,380
You're the pride of our Katsushika station.

284
00:15:59,380 --> 00:16:03,860
Actually, when I saw your work at the
Katsushika station's art exhibition,

285
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:06,080
I thought, "Could this be the one?"

286
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:11,160
Yet the way you kept my work
walled off from public view

287
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:12,900
is a mystery, I suppose.

288
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:16,520
Someone who wins a prize doesn't worry about such trivial things,
does he?

289
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:17,580
Chief.

290
00:16:17,580 --> 00:16:18,860
By the way, Ryotsu-kun...

291
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:21,160
I came to talk to you about something.

292
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:22,420
A favor?

293
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:25,200
Actually, about your first
work that won the gold prize,

294
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:28,840
the regional headquarters chief has
said he very much wants to buy it.

295
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:30,140
What do you think?

296
00:16:30,140 --> 00:16:31,840
The regional headquarters chief, you see.

297
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:35,500
Understood. I'll accept that.

298
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:36,220
Really?

299
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:38,360
Ohara, that's wonderful, just wonderful.

300
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:40,360
This will save face for me too.

301
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:41,700
That's great.

302
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:44,480
In exchange, I have one condition.

303
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:51,780
No, no,
how many times do I have to tell you?

304
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:55,080
Press your cheeks together tightly,
really stick together.

305
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:57,520
Like this?

306
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:02,300
Are they really going to
paint us looking like this?

307
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:05,000
No, that's wrong again.

308
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:09,820
Even so, the one we're dealing
with is a gold-prize-winning artist.

309
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:13,000
We ordinary people have
no choice but to obey.

310
00:17:14,660 --> 00:17:15,700
Got it.

311
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:17,640
This guy's in the way.

312
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:19,960
Hey, Ryotsu!

313
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,540
Don't you want to?

314
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:24,900
Then maybe I'll just stop painting,
little me.

315
00:17:25,820 --> 00:17:27,580
Ohara, we have to bear with this.

316
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:28,720
Patience, patience.

317
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:31,940
Unpleasant? Not at all.

318
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:34,360
We'll do exactly as
the teacher wishes, so...

319
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:37,400
Well then.

320
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:40,160
Maybe I'll have them
strike a pose like this.

321
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:42,400
Ryotsu

322
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:44,440
Matsuo! Harako! Y-yes!

323
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:47,640
Th-this is fine, Myotsu-kun.

324
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:50,180
You're getting into the groove now, you two.

325
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:51,560
Well then, next is...

326
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:08,620
Good, yes, just like that. Don't move.

327
00:18:17,420 --> 00:18:20,460
If that's the case, couldn't he have
used someone other than us as models?

328
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:24,200
Isn't that just how art works, Ohara?

329
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:26,940
Anyway, let's hurry and forget about that.

330
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:27,580
Yes, that's right.

331
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:32,500
Hello, this is Ryotsu, the gold
prize winner from the art exhibition.

332
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:34,980
Yes, I'd really like you
to paint a picture of me.

333
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:36,680
Well, and what about Yo-san?

334
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:38,840
Just a moment, please.

335
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:42,000
Hello, this is Ryotsu,
the gold prize winner.

336
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:43,380
Is it since the exhibition?

337
00:18:43,730 --> 00:18:45,620
The power of a gold prize is amazing,
isn't it?

338
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:47,700
Orders are pouring in, aren't they?

339
00:18:48,070 --> 00:18:49,560
Excuse me, is anyone home?

340
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:53,740
Is Mr. Ryotsu, the teacher, here?

341
00:18:55,980 --> 00:18:57,960
That's me.

342
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,340
My apologies.

343
00:19:00,930 --> 00:19:04,320
Congratulations on winning the
gold prize at the art exhibition.

344
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:07,140
I'm a painter.

345
00:19:07,140 --> 00:19:08,980
My name is Rodriguez Ito.

346
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:09,440
Nice to meet you.

347
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:12,680
So, what do you want with me?

348
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:14,660
Well, actually, Sensei,

349
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:19,420
I would really like to be
allowed to assist you, Sensei.

350
00:19:19,420 --> 00:19:21,080
I've got enough help.

351
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:24,200
Don't be so cold.

352
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:26,780
Sensei, let me help you.

353
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:29,920
What are you talking about?

354
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:31,900
Besides,
I'd be fine without someone like you.

355
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:35,580
Even my recent selected painting
sold for five million yen.

356
00:19:37,580 --> 00:19:40,360
Don't tell me you actually
sold it like that, Sensei?

357
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:42,280
Well, not yet.

358
00:19:42,280 --> 00:19:46,000
Good. Amateurs like you are such a hassle.

359
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:50,760
In that case, you first make
a lithograph from that painting.

360
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:51,580
Lithograph?

361
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:54,000
It's stone printing.

362
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
With this, you can reproduce the
painting as many times as you like.

363
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,680
Then you sell each one for 10,000 yen.

364
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:02,100
And you say it's a limited edition of 500.

365
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:05,500
Sell 500 and you've got
5 million yen in no time.

366
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:07,720
And you still keep the original.

367
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:12,200
Say it's limited to 500, but print 50,000.
Nobody will ever know.

368
00:20:13,280 --> 00:20:16,380
Well, Sensei,
have you decided to team up with me?

369
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:21,820
Rodriguez-kun, I'm starting to
feel like we'll get along well.

370
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:24,040
You finally understand, don't you.

371
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:28,860
Then first, let's tie up with a department
store and hold a solo exhibition, shall we?

372
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:31,340
Since we're at it,
if there's any risk at the venue,

373
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:34,540
I guess birds of a feather flock together.

374
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:38,940
That's how the senior's popularity,
thanks to Mr. Rodriguez Ito,

375
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:41,240
kept soaring on bluster and sales skill.

376
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:43,420
His solo exhibition drew a huge crowd.

377
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,780
Related merchandise sold like hotcakes.

378
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:48,440
He also developed a new game,

379
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:52,480
and painted a 500-meter mural at the Expo venue,
and the senior

380
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:55,620
is now firmly established
as a charismatic painter.

381
00:20:56,300 --> 00:21:00,280
Crowds of reporters swarmed our
police box and his family home.

382
00:21:02,100 --> 00:21:03,940
And next, it's Kankichi Ryotsu.

383
00:21:03,940 --> 00:21:04,880
Hello.

384
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:06,280
Looks like you're on TV again, senpai.

385
00:21:06,280 --> 00:21:09,140
What do you think about this case,
Mr. Ryotsu?

386
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:11,460
I'll put it bluntly, though.

387
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:14,400
The wife is partly to blame, too.

388
00:21:16,320 --> 00:21:16,680
And also,

389
00:21:20,340 --> 00:21:22,800
Sensei, please be a little more
careful about your behavior.

390
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:26,060
Don't worry. The public and the media

391
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:28,580
are all on the side of
the genius painter Ryotsu.

392
00:21:29,180 --> 00:21:33,480
They may be on your side now, but who knows
when they'll turn on you and start attacking.

393
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:36,640
From now on, please focus only on painting.

394
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:38,120
So then,

395
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:42,480
I've decided I want to
test my abilities overseas.

396
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:43,700
Overseas?

397
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:54,400
I'll hold solo exhibitions all over the world and return from overseas as Ryotsu,
the world's artist, so look forward to it!

398
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:57,380
Sensei, please reconsider!

399
00:21:58,580 --> 00:22:02,620
Your style is so domestic,
it'll be really tough if you go abroad.

400
00:22:02,620 --> 00:22:03,620
Hey, Sensei.

401
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:05,840
Maybe we can talk, talk about it?

402
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:07,760
No way, reconsider it!

403
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:08,740
Shut up already!

404
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:10,720
Sensei.

405
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:16,040
With my skills,
I'm sure I'll succeed overseas too.

406
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:18,140
I'm telling you, no way!

407
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:22,580
No good, let's find the next newcomer.

408
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:25,500
Yes, this is Ito speaking.

409
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:28,400
What? An elementary school student
got into the Gokaten exhibition?

410
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:28,880
Amazing.

411
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:35,300
And then Senpai held solo exhibitions one after another,
in New York, Paris,

412
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:37,980
but that turned out to be his downfall.

413
00:22:38,740 --> 00:22:42,320
The media in each
country tore him to shreds.

414
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:48,500
Ryotsu's paintings? That's just graffiti.
Mark my words, they're worthless.

415
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:50,880
Japan caught wind of the news too,

416
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:54,420
and word spread across the country
that his paintings were just bad.

417
00:22:55,500 --> 00:23:02,040
His standing collapsed. Senpai's getting hammered
hard since the failed overseas solo exhibitions.

418
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:07,560
His reputation has plummeted. Man, this is awful.
It's like the fate of a one-hit wonder.

419
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:18,640
Well, I kind of expected it. It was on the morning news too, you know.
Apparently the people who bought Ryo-chan's painting rushed to the department stores and galleries to complain.

420
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:19,500
Whoa!

421
00:23:19,620 --> 00:23:23,170
Hmph, just because he got praised a little,
he got cocky,

422
00:23:23,220 --> 00:23:24,420
so he got what was coming to him.

423
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:26,720
But I feel a little sorry for him.

424
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:30,020
I wonder what the senior is up to right now,
and where.

425
00:23:34,740 --> 00:23:37,160
Come on, step right up,
come on over and take a look!

426
00:23:37,300 --> 00:23:39,028
Here we have the gold prize
winner from the art exhibition,

427
00:23:39,078 --> 00:23:42,280
the work of the award-winning painter Ryotsu.
Come and see!

428
00:23:42,420 --> 00:23:45,380
Here from the corner department store,
Shirokiya, Kurokiya, and Akakiya!

429
00:23:45,380 --> 00:23:48,440
Then the gal with the lipstick on says,
"Please, can I have one?"

430
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:51,040
They're easily worth fifty or a hundred thousand yen,
you amateurs.

431
00:24:25,180 --> 00:24:28,540
Thank you for watching.

432
00:24:28,560 --> 00:24:30,580
Playing it cool with one hand,

433
00:24:30,580 --> 00:24:33,340
a beef bowl with extra sauce,
cloudy and soupy.

434
00:24:34,100 --> 00:24:36,660
Overtime after overtime,
and all the frustration,

435
00:24:36,660 --> 00:24:40,280
ylang-ylang clears it all away.

436
00:24:43,680 --> 00:24:46,360
Every day's no-problem-blem.

437
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:50,080
After passing through a hot shower,

438
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:53,220
every day's no-problem-blem.

439
00:24:53,220 --> 00:24:56,640
the Anmin pillow restores your energy.

440
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:02,740
Every day's no-problem-brain.

441
00:25:02,740 --> 00:25:06,260
I love myself just like this.

442
00:25:06,260 --> 00:25:09,460
Every day's no-problem-brain.

443
00:25:09,460 --> 00:25:13,060
Hearts are flying on Monday.

444
00:25:13,060 --> 00:25:17,440
Anmin, Anmin, no-problem-brain.

445
00:25:19,080 --> 00:25:21,800
Senpai, it's a real emergency!

446
00:25:23,220 --> 00:25:24,720
Eve came down with a fever and collapsed,

447
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:25,900
and now she keeps having nightmares.

448
00:25:25,900 --> 00:25:28,260
She keeps talking about the ring
I gave her when we were kids.

449
00:25:28,260 --> 00:25:30,280
Please help me look for it too, senpai.

450
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:32,140
I'm sure I buried it somewhere.

451
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:35,020
Next time: The Honda Family Clan 2

452
00:25:35,020 --> 00:25:37,400
Eve's treasure, please.

453
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:40,700
Over there, there are turtles. (Kame-ari)

454
00:25:41,920 --> 00:25:44,020
Well, I'm sure there's Kame-ari.

455
00:25:45,540 --> 00:25:49,180
Everyone, come on over to our town!

456
00:25:50,380 --> 00:25:50,780
Thank you.

457
00:25:53,220 --> 00:25:54,000
Thank you for watching.

